# =============================================================================
# TEX-TAILOR FRONTEND ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION
# =============================================================================
# This file contains environment variables for the Vue.js frontend application
# Copy this file to .env in the frontend/ directory and fill in your values.
# 
# IMPORTANT: Only VITE_ prefixed variables are available in the browser!
# Never put sensitive information (API keys, secrets) in frontend env files.
# =============================================================================

# =============================================================================
# API CONFIGURATION (REQUIRED)
# =============================================================================

# Backend API URL - This is the ONLY variable the frontend needs
# 
# For Local Development:
# VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3001
#
# For Production (update with your actual backend URL):
# VITE_API_URL=https://your-backend.onrender.com
#
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3001

# =============================================================================
# DEVELOPMENT NOTES
# =============================================================================

# The frontend has environment-specific files:
# - .env.development (for npm run dev) - uses localhost:3001
# - .env.production (for npm run build) - uses your production backend URL
# 
# This .env.example serves as a template for both environments.

# =============================================================================
# DEPLOYMENT INSTRUCTIONS
# =============================================================================

# For Vercel Deployment:
# 1. Set VITE_API_URL in Vercel dashboard environment variables
# 2. Point it to your Render backend: https://your-service.onrender.com
# 3. No other frontend environment variables are needed

# For Local Development:
# 1. Copy this file to .env (in frontend/ directory)
# 2. Set VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3001
# 3. Start backend server first (npm run server from frontend directory)
# 4. Start frontend (npm run dev:client from frontend directory)

# =============================================================================
# SECURITY REMINDER
# =============================================================================

# Frontend environment variables are PUBLIC and bundled into your JavaScript!
# - Never put API keys, database URLs, or secrets here
# - Only put public configuration like API endpoints
# - Sensitive data belongs in the backend .env file
